摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"A DSH plugin that draws a .superworker/ pipeline record as a work panel, and answers the pipeline's words inside a session.","id":"gh:1426226250","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-superworker","slug":"infraredsqy/dsh-superworker","topics":["agent-workflow","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","git-merge","pipeline","superworker","visualization"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"A DSH plugin that draws a .superworker/ pipeline record as a work panel, and answers the pipeline's "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"words inside a session."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-superworker"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"`dsh-superworker` is a DeepSeek Harness plugin\nthat renders a `.superworker/` pipeline record as a p"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"anel in the DSH Web UI."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"The host half reads the record (`.superworker/`) of the current session's workspace and serves it be"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"hind a\ngateway; the browser half draws it as the **Superworker** panel in the sidebar. Everything on"},{"id":"p5s3","text":" screen —\ninstructions, node details, the map of who owes whom, the issue pool — comes from that rec"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"ord, and\nwrites from the panel go back to the same place."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"In a session the pipeline is also reachable as the agent-facing `superworker` tool: it answers the\np"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"ipeline's words in place. A session whose workspace holds a `.superworker/` record sees the tool fro"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"m its\nfirst step; anywhere else it appears only after one of the `sw-*` skills loads — until then th"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"at\nsession's request header stays exactly as it would be without this plugin."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Status"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Early, and tied to the DSH developer preview. The manifest declares an `engines.dsh` range, and DSH\n"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"refuses to install or boot the plugin outside that range (`incompatible-version`, with an opt-in\nexe"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"mption command). The range follows DSH's breaking line: any rc within 0.2.x is admitted, and it\nmove"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"s when DSH moves to 0.3."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"The `.superworker/` record it draws is early and moving fast: expect breaking changes in its shape."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Prerequisites: a DSH install with a profile to install into, and a workspace that holds a `.superwor"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"ker/`\npipeline record. The panel's writes are answered in place by its host half (the engine's own w"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"ords\nlayer), so there is no command to install and no `PATH` entry to arrange. The panel\nreads the w"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"orkspace of the session you have selected; with no session selected it says so."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Download the `.tgz` from this repo's Releases\nand point DSH at the file:"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"The package ships prebuilt — installing runs no build steps. pnpm may print a few `missing peer`\nwar"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"nings: those packages are provided by DSH itself and resolve at runtime, so the warnings can be\nigno"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"red. The version policy and the third route (installing from git) live in\ndocs/publish.md."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## What you get"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"- a **Superworker** entry in the Web UI sidebar: views over the record — the map, details,\ninstructi"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"ons, the issue pool, and the panel's own settings\n- a **Superworker settings** section in the DSH se"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"ttings: whether archived instructions show,\nwhether closed issues show\n- to verify an install: `dsh "},{"id":"p16s4","text":"--profile <name> --dump-config`, and look for the\n`# == dsh-superworker` section"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Development"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"`npm test` builds both products and runs both suites, the plugin's and the engine package's. What\nea"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"ch file pins, and what is walked by hand instead, is in tests/AGENTS.md;\ndocs/publish.md carries the"},{"id":"p19s3","text":" hand pass, and `tools/testbed/` boots an isolated\nDSH instance for it."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"The repository map and ground rules live in AGENTS.md. Read\ndocs/design-principles.md before touchin"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"g the UI, and\ndocs/publish.md before shipping a version."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Contact"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Support for running this in your own pipeline, feedback on how it went, and commercial questions\ngo "},{"id":"p22s2","text":"to infraredsaw@gmail.com. Bugs and feature requests are better\nfiled as issues — that way the next p"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"erson\nwho hits the same wall finds them."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"MIT"}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
